# Look
option.LOOK_PRESET=Look
option.LOOK_PRESET.comment=Picks how light and color are rendered. Natural: a plain Minecraft-like look that is easy on the eyes. Vivid: like SEUS Renewed / PTGI, with contrast between sun and shade, warm sunlight against blue-green shade, green bounce light from the grass and highlights that reach near white (saturation and bloom stay modest). Daylight: Vivid lighting plus a deeper blue sky, greener grass and more sunlit relief, for punchy clear days. Summer Sky: bright, airy midsummer days with deep blue down to the horizon, lush greens and warm sun. Golden Hour: warm, low-sun light all day with soft bloom. Teal & Orange: the classic film look, shade and grass toward teal, highlights, wood and soil toward orange. Bleach Bypass: muted colors and hard contrast (strong contrast, tiring over long sessions). Cross Process: yellow-green highlights and blue shadows (strong color and contrast). Game: clear, saturated colors with lifted dark areas for easy play. Saturation, Contrast, Exposure Compensation, Bloom, Bloomy Fog, Sky Light Occlusion, Sky Ambient Saturation and Fog Density multiply the preset values (exposure is added). Color Grading settings also stack on top of the preset. Custom: set the preset-only values under Post Processing > Color > Custom Look
value.LOOK_PRESET.0=Custom
value.LOOK_PRESET.1=Natural
value.LOOK_PRESET.2=Vivid
value.LOOK_PRESET.3=Daylight
value.LOOK_PRESET.4=Summer Sky
value.LOOK_PRESET.5=Golden Hour
value.LOOK_PRESET.6=Teal & Orange
value.LOOK_PRESET.7=Bleach Bypass
value.LOOK_PRESET.8=Cross Process
value.LOOK_PRESET.9=Game (Vivid)
option.LOOK_LUT=LUT
option.LOOK_LUT.comment=A color LUT applied last (3D LUT on the display values after the tone map). Stacks after the look preset and Color Grading. User LUT: replace shaders/textures/look/user_lut.png with your own (the identity image graded in an image editor, or a .cube converted with tools/gen_look_lut.py; see docs/guides/profiles.md). Sun and Shade Split: warmer sun, bluer-green shade, bright greens toward yellow-green. Film: slightly lower contrast, warm and less saturated highlights. The film-like LUTs approximate the characteristics described in the makers' public data sheets; no manufacturer data is used. Portra-like: lower contrast, lifted blacks, soft warm color. Ektar-like: vivid reds and blues, firm contrast. Vision3 500T-like: the blue cast of tungsten cinema film used in daylight, soft gradation. Velvia-like: high saturation and contrast, deep blue skies and greens (strong color and contrast). Provia-like: faithful, slightly vivid. Eterna-like: calm low saturation and soft contrast
value.LOOK_LUT.0=None
value.LOOK_LUT.1=User LUT
value.LOOK_LUT.2=Sun and Shade Split
value.LOOK_LUT.3=Film
value.LOOK_LUT.4=Portra-like
value.LOOK_LUT.5=Ektar-like
value.LOOK_LUT.6=Vision3 500T-like
value.LOOK_LUT.7=Velvia-like
value.LOOK_LUT.8=Provia-like
value.LOOK_LUT.9=Eterna-like
option.LOOK_LUT_STRENGTH=LUT Strength
option.LOOK_LUT_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the LUT is applied (mixed with the original color)
screen.LOOK_CUSTOM=Custom Look
screen.LOOK_CUSTOM.comment=Only used when Look is Custom. Sets the values that only the presets have. Everything else uses the regular options (Saturation, Contrast, ...)
option.LOOK_C_SKY_AMBIENT=Sky Ambient Strength
option.LOOK_C_SKY_AMBIENT.comment=Strength of the sky light that fills the shade. Lower values increase the difference between sun and shade (the sky itself keeps its brightness). Natural 1, Vivid 0.8
option.LOOK_C_SKY_SATURATION=Sky Color Saturation
option.LOOK_C_SKY_SATURATION.comment=How deep the sky blue is (both the sky and the sky ambient light). Natural 1, Vivid 1.08
option.LOOK_C_SUN_WARMTH=Sunlight Warmth
option.LOOK_C_SUN_WARMTH.comment=How much the direct sunlight is shifted toward warm colors (brightness is kept). Splits the warm sun from the blue sky light in the shade. The sky, clouds and sun disc keep their colors. 1 = a 5000K color against 6500K. Natural 0, Vivid 0.85
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE=Bounce Light Strength
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE.comment=Strength of the bounce light (light from surfaces hit by GI rays). The sky light is unchanged, so only the bounce from grass and walls gets stronger. GI Strength multiplies this. Natural 1, Vivid 1.6
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE_SATURATION=Bounce Light Saturation
option.LOOK_C_BOUNCE_SATURATION.comment=Saturation of the bounce light (light from surfaces hit by GI rays). Higher values tint shade, birch trunks and cave entrances green from the grass. Brightness is unchanged. Natural 1, Vivid 1.5
option.LOOK_C_HIGHLIGHT=Highlight Range
option.LOOK_C_HIGHLIGHT.comment=Widens the brightness differences above middle gray (the dark side is unchanged). Higher values let white clouds and sunlit surfaces reach near white. Natural 1.1, Vivid 1.6
option.LOOK_C_DARK_LIFT=Shadow Lift
option.LOOK_C_DARK_LIFT.comment=Brightness of the darkest tones after the tone map. AgX expects a display with a 2.2 power curve, but the output is re-encoded with the piecewise sRGB curve, so on 2.2 displays dark areas sink by 1-3 EV and crush to black. 1 restores them (midtones and highlights barely change). Natural 0, Vivid 0.5
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_SPREAD=Bloom Spread
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_SPREAD.comment=How far the glow around lights spreads. Lower values keep it close to the light so shade is not lifted by the glow. Natural 0.82, Vivid 0.75
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_FOG_CLEAR=Clear-Weather Bloomy Fog
option.LOOK_C_BLOOM_FOG_CLEAR.comment=How much wide glow is applied to distant terrain in clear weather (1 in rain). Natural 0.35, Vivid 0.35

# Block lighting
option.VOXEL_VOLUME=Voxel Volume
option.VOXEL_VOLUME.comment=Size of the voxel area around the player used for colored light and light shadows. Larger costs more VRAM.
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.0=128x64x128
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.1=192x96x192
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.2=256x128x256
value.VOXEL_VOLUME.3=384x128x384
option.FLOODFILL=Colored Floodfill
option.FLOODFILL.comment=Colored light that spreads through voxels. Used as indirect light when light shadows are on.
option.FLOODFILL_STRENGTH=Floodfill Indirect Strength
option.FLOODFILL_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the floodfill bounce light when light source shadows are enabled.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BOUNCE=Block Light Wall Bounce
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BOUNCE.comment=How much block light bounces off walls and picks up their color (a red room tints the light red). 0 = no bounce.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Block Light Brightness
option.BLOCKLIGHT_WARMTH=Block Light Warmth
option.BLOCKLIGHT_WARMTH.comment=0 = neutral white fire light, 1 = warm orange like vanilla.
option.LIGHT_FALLOFF_MODE=Light Reach
option.LIGHT_FALLOFF_MODE.comment=How far the light of each light source reaches. Level: proportional to the light level and cut off near the end, so low level sources (magma blocks, amethyst, candles) end in a visible ring after a few blocks. Light Amount: proportional to the square root of brightness x level, and the light fades to zero at the end without a ring. Brightness close to bright sources is nearly the same in both. Light Amount lights a larger area per source and is heavier in scenes with many dim sources.
value.LIGHT_FALLOFF_MODE.0=Level
value.LIGHT_FALLOFF_MODE.1=Light Amount
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MAJOR_MAX=Main Light Reach
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MAJOR_MAX.comment=With Light Reach set to Light Amount, how far main light sources (torches, lanterns, glowstone, sea lanterns, froglights) reach at full brightness (blocks). Larger lights more distant floors and walls but costs more.
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MAJOR_MIN=Main Light Reach Min
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MAJOR_MIN.comment=With Light Reach set to Light Amount, the shortest reach of main light sources (blocks).
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MINOR_MAX=Dim Light Reach
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MINOR_MAX.comment=With Light Reach set to Light Amount, how far dim or clustered light sources (ores, amethyst, magma, glow lichen, cave vines, lava, portals) reach at full brightness (blocks). These often come in large groups, so larger values cost more.
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MINOR_MIN=Dim Light Reach Min
option.LIGHT_RANGE_MINOR_MIN.comment=With Light Reach set to Light Amount, the shortest reach of dim or clustered light sources (blocks). Larger lets dim light fade out more gradually but costs more in scenes with many dim sources (amethyst geodes, glow lichen caves).
option.LIGHT_FLICKER=Light Flicker
option.LIGHT_FLICKER.comment=Subtle flicker on fire based lights.
option.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS=Mineral Block Glow
option.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.comment=Lapis, emerald, diamond, gold, redstone and amethyst blocks. Off = vanilla, Glow Only = the surface glows without lighting its surroundings, Light Source = also emits a dim colored light with shadows.
value.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.0=Off
value.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.1=Glow Only
value.DECORATIVE_BLOCK_LIGHTS.2=Light Source
option.DECOR_LAPIS=Lapis Block
option.DECOR_LAPIS.comment=Makes lapis blocks glow. No effect while Mineral Block Glow is Off.
option.DECOR_EMERALD=Emerald Block
option.DECOR_EMERALD.comment=Makes emerald blocks glow.
option.DECOR_DIAMOND=Diamond Block
option.DECOR_DIAMOND.comment=Makes diamond blocks glow.
option.DECOR_GOLD=Gold Block
option.DECOR_GOLD.comment=Makes gold blocks glow.
option.DECOR_REDSTONE=Redstone Block
option.DECOR_REDSTONE.comment=Makes redstone blocks glow.
option.DECOR_AMETHYST=Amethyst Block
option.DECOR_AMETHYST.comment=Makes amethyst blocks and budding amethyst glow.
option.DECOR_BRIGHTNESS=Mineral Block Brightness
option.DECOR_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How brightly the mineral blocks glow, and how strongly they light their surroundings. 0 = no glow.
option.DECOR_SATURATION=Mineral Block Color
option.DECOR_SATURATION.comment=Color strength of the mineral blocks' glow and light. Brightness stays about the same. 0 = white, 1 = the mineral's color, 2 = close to the pure primary color (amethyst only gets a slightly deeper purple).
option.LIGHT_SHADOWS=Light Source Shadows
option.LIGHT_SHADOWS.comment=Ray traces the strongest nearby lights so blocks, players and entities cast shadows from placed lights.
option.LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Placed Light Shadow Darkness
option.LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by placed lights are, including dropped, burning and glowing entities. 0 = no shadows, 1 = full shadows.
option.LIGHT_TRACE_COUNT=Traced Lights per Pixel
option.LIGHT_TRACE_SPLIT=Shadow Rays in Dense Areas
option.LIGHT_TRACE_SPLIT.comment=In pixels lit by more lights than Traced Lights per Pixel, only the much brighter lights are traced every frame and the other rays go to lights picked at random in proportion to their brightness. Where many lights of similar brightness sit together (amethyst clusters), fewer traced lights give less shadow noise. Same cost.
option.LIGHT_TRACE_RES=Trace Resolution
option.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.comment=Resolution of the light shadow trace. Lower is faster but noisier.
value.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.1=Full
value.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.2=Half
value.LIGHT_TRACE_RES.4=Quarter
option.LIGHT_SHAPE_TRACE=Block Shape Occlusion
option.LIGHT_SHAPE_TRACE.comment=Slabs, fences and walls cast shadows with their real shape.
option.LIGHT_SOURCE_SIZE=Light Source Size
option.LIGHT_SOURCE_SIZE.comment=Larger sources give softer shadow edges.
option.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE=Emissive Face Shape
option.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.comment=How light-emitting blocks such as sea lanterns light nearby surfaces. Whole Face: the entire face glows evenly. Glowing Area: only the bright rectangle of the texture glows, so dark frames darken the contact line (no extra cost). Texture Mask: also follows the pattern inside the texture (heavier close to light blocks).
value.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.0=Whole Face
value.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.1=Glowing Area
value.LIGHT_EMISSION_MASK_MODE.2=Texture Mask
option.LIGHT_TRANSLUCENT_TINT=Stained Glass Tint
option.LIGHT_TRANSLUCENT_TINT.comment=Light passing through stained glass is colored.
option.LIGHT_TRANSLUCENT_TINT_SATURATION=Stained Glass Block Light Color
option.LIGHT_TRANSLUCENT_TINT_SATURATION.comment=Color strength of block light passing through stained glass and other see-through blocks except water (ice, slime, honey). Brightness stays about the same. 0 = no color (the light only dims), 1 = the glass color.
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR=Block Light Specular
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR_OCCLUSION=Specular Light Occlusion
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR_OCCLUSION.comment=Keeps lights hidden behind walls from showing up in metal and other shiny surfaces. Slightly heavier when many shiny surfaces are on screen.
option.LIGHT_DENOISE=Light Denoiser
value.LIGHT_DENOISE.0=Off
value.LIGHT_DENOISE.1=Temporal
value.LIGHT_DENOISE.2=Temporal + Spatial
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_OCCLUSION=Entity Occlusion
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_OCCLUSION.comment=Mobs and block entities block placed light sources. Renders entities in the shadow pass (costly).
option.LIGHT_PLAYER_OCCLUSION=Player Occlusion
option.LIGHT_PLAYER_OCCLUSION.comment=Your player blocks placed light sources.
option.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE=Entity Occlusion Method
option.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE.comment=How players and mobs block light. Voxel: half-block boxes (fast, blocky shadows). Triangle: the actual model shape, including transparent parts.
value.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE.0=Voxel
value.LIGHT_OCCLUSION_MODE.1=Triangle
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_TRIANGLES=Entity Triangle Limit
option.LIGHT_ENTITY_TRIANGLES.comment=Triangles kept for the Triangle method. 1024 are reserved for your player. Entities beyond the limit fall back to voxel boxes.
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOWS=Light Contact Shadows
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=Screen space shadows that add details too small for the voxel grid.
option.LIGHT_CULL_MODE=Light Selection Over Limit
option.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.comment=Which lights stay when a bin or the total light count is over its limit. Arrival Order: keeps the lights registered first; different lights drop out each frame and flicker. Nearest: keeps the closest lights. Brightness x Distance: keeps the lights that contribute the most (default). Nearest and Brightness x Distance fade lights at the cutoff over a few frames and align bins to the world grid, so the selection does not change as you walk. Scenes under the limits look and perform the same.
value.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.0=Arrival Order
value.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.1=Nearest
value.LIGHT_CULL_MODE.2=Brightness x Distance
option.LIGHT_MAX_COUNT=Total Light Limit
option.LIGHT_MAX_COUNT.comment=Lights handled as direct light per frame. Lights over the limit are dropped farthest first (their floodfill light stays). Higher costs more binning and tracing candidates. Matters for nether glowstone and light-heavy towns.
option.LIGHT_BIN_LIGHTS=Lights per Bin
option.LIGHT_BIN_LIGHTS.comment=Lights kept in one 8x8x8-block bin. Less important lights drop out beyond it. Higher makes pixels in dense light clusters check more lights. Above 64 uses about 10 MB more VRAM.
option.LIGHT_TRACE_STEPS=Light Shadow Ray Length
option.LIGHT_TRACE_STEPS.comment=Maximum blocks a light shadow ray walks. Too low cuts the shadows of long-reaching lights and leaks light. Most rays reach their light first, so raising it costs little.
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR_COUNT=Specular Lights
option.LIGHT_SPECULAR_COUNT.comment=Lights that add specular highlights per pixel (strongest first). Too few shows lines where highlights switch on floors lit by many lights. Higher costs more in opaque shading.
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOW_COUNT=Contact Shadow Lights
option.LIGHT_CONTACT_SHADOW_COUNT.comment=Lights that get screen-space contact shadows per pixel (strongest first). Higher is slower.
option.HAND_LIGHT=Handheld Light
option.HAND_LIGHT.comment=Holding a light source lights up the surroundings (both hands).
option.HAND_LIGHT_RAYS=Handheld Light Rays
option.HAND_LIGHT_RAYS.comment=Ray traced shadows for handheld lights.
option.HAND_LIGHT_SS_SHADOWS=Handheld Light Contact Shadows
option.HAND_LIGHT_SS_SHADOWS.comment=Screen space shadows from your hand and nearby entities.
option.HAND_LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Handheld Light Brightness
option.HAND_LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Handheld Light Shadow Darkness
option.HAND_LIGHT_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by a handheld light are. 0 = no shadows. At 0.6 the direct shadow is full and some bounced light reaches it; above that only the bounced light shrinks, 1 = no bounce light from the handheld light.
option.ENTITY_LIGHTS=Entity Lights
option.ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment=Master switch for dynamic light from entities.
option.ITEM_LIGHTS=Dropped Item Lights
option.ITEM_LIGHTS.comment=Dropped light items (torches, lava buckets...) emit light.
option.PROJECTILE_LIGHTS=Projectile Lights
option.PROJECTILE_LIGHTS.comment=Spectral arrows, fireballs and fireworks emit light.
option.BURNING_ENTITY_LIGHTS=Burning Entity Lights
option.BURNING_ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment=Entities on fire emit light.
option.GLOWING_ENTITY_LIGHTS=Glowing Entity Lights
option.GLOWING_ENTITY_LIGHTS.comment=Blazes, glow squids, magma cubes, end crystals and flashing TNT emit light.
option.CHARGED_CREEPER_LIGHT=Charged Creeper / Wither Armor Light
option.CHARGED_CREEPER_LIGHT.comment=The electric swirl of a charged creeper and of the wither's armor lights its surroundings blue-white while it is shown. Soft light through Colored Floodfill (no shadows, almost no cost).
option.CHARGED_CREEPER_LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Charged Creeper / Wither Armor Light Strength
option.CHARGED_CREEPER_LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How strongly the electric swirl lights its surroundings. Higher values light farther. Does not change how bright the swirl itself looks.

# Shadows & GI
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=Keep this at or above the voxel volume radius (64 / 96 / 128 / 192).
option.shadowDistanceRenderMul=Shadow Render Optimization
value.shadowDistanceRenderMul.-1.0=Off
value.shadowDistanceRenderMul.1.0=On
option.entityShadowDistanceMul=Entity Shadow Distance
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Path Rotation
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow Filter
value.SHADOW_FILTER.0=Hard
value.SHADOW_FILTER.1=PCF
value.SHADOW_FILTER.2=PCSS
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES=Shadow Samples
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SUN_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Sun Shadow Darkness
option.SUN_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by the sun are. 0 = no shadows, 1 = full shadows. Cloud shadows are not affected.
option.MOON_SHADOW_STRENGTH=Moon Shadow Darkness
option.MOON_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How dark the shadows cast by the moon and the End light are. 0 = no shadows, 1 = full shadows.
option.SHADOW_COLORED=Colored Shadows
option.SHADOW_COLORED.comment=Stained glass and water cast colored sun shadows.
option.SHADOW_COLORED_SATURATION=Stained Glass Sunlight Color
option.SHADOW_COLORED_SATURATION.comment=Color strength of sun and moon light passing through stained glass and other see-through blocks except water (ice, slime, honey), in shadows and light shafts. Brightness stays about the same. 0 = no color (the light only dims), 1 = the glass color.
option.ENTITY_SHADOWS=Entity Shadows
option.BLOCK_ENTITY_SHADOWS=Block Entity Shadows
option.SCREEN_SPACE_SHADOWS=Contact Shadows
option.AO_MODE=Ambient Occlusion
value.AO_MODE.0=Off
value.AO_MODE.1=SSAO
value.AO_MODE.2=GTAO
option.AO_STRENGTH=AO Strength
option.GI_MODE=Global Illumination
value.GI_MODE.0=Off
value.GI_MODE.1=RSM
value.GI_MODE.2=Screen Space
value.GI_MODE.3=Voxel Ray Traced
option.GI_SAMPLES=GI Samples
option.GI_STRENGTH=GI Strength
option.GI_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the bounce light (and, with screen-space or voxel ray tracing, the sky light). Higher values brighten shade, downward faces and rooms and reduce the contrast with sunlight. The effect is scaled per method so the same value looks similar (voxel x1, RSM x0.75, screen-space x0.5).
option.GI_MULTI_BOUNCE=Multiple Bounces
option.GI_MULTI_BOUNCE.comment=How much of the previous frame's GI is fed back into the surfaces GI rays hit, so light bounces again with every frame. Lets light reach deeper into cave entrances and rooms at almost no cost. 0 = single bounce, 1 = physically correct (screen-space and voxel ray tracing only).
option.GI_SKY_BOUNCE_STRENGTH=Sky Light Bounce
option.GI_SKY_BOUNCE_STRENGTH.comment=How much sun, moon and sky light bounces off the surfaces GI rays hit. Higher values let light coming through a window light up the room more. 0 = no bounce of this light.
option.GI_SKY_BOUNCE_SATURATION=Sky Light Bounce Color
option.GI_SKY_BOUNCE_SATURATION.comment=How strongly the color of the surface hit (a red carpet, green grass) tints the bounced sun, moon and sky light. Brightness stays about the same. 0 = gray bounce.
option.GI_BLOCK_BOUNCE_STRENGTH=Block Light Bounce
option.GI_BLOCK_BOUNCE_STRENGTH.comment=How much block light bounces off the surfaces GI rays hit and off the walls next to lit surfaces (multiplies Block Light Wall Bounce). 0 = no bounce of this light.
option.GI_BLOCK_BOUNCE_SATURATION=Block Light Bounce Color
option.GI_BLOCK_BOUNCE_SATURATION.comment=How strongly the color of the surface hit (a red carpet, a colored wall) tints the bounced block light. Brightness stays about the same. 0 = gray bounce.
option.GI_SKY_OCCLUSION=Sky Light Occlusion
option.GI_SKY_OCCLUSION.comment=How much of the sky light is occluded by the GI rays. 1 = light only comes from directions that see the sky (eaves, cave entrances and the back of rooms get darker, and openings show their direction). 0 = occlusion from the skylight level only (no direction, counted twice with the bounce). The default 0.5 keeps rooms and cave entrances from getting too dark (at 1 they are too dark even with multiple bounces). Screen-space and voxel ray tracing only. Multiplies the Look preset value (1 with Natural)
option.GI_GROUND_REPLACE=Ground Bounce Replacement
option.GI_GROUND_REPLACE.comment=How much of the gray ground bounce built into the sky ambient is replaced by the real ground color picked up by GI (green on grass). 1 = physically correct (shade and downward faces take the ground color and get darker). 0 = keeps the gray ground bounce (brighter, gray shade; the bounce is counted twice).
option.GI_RES=GI Resolution
value.GI_RES.1=Full
value.GI_RES.2=Half
option.GI_DENOISE=GI Denoiser
value.GI_DENOISE.0=Off
value.GI_DENOISE.1=Temporal
value.GI_DENOISE.2=Temporal + Spatial
option.GI_HISTORY_MAX=GI History Length
option.GI_HISTORY_MAX.comment=Maximum number of past frames GI averages over. Longer is cleaner when still; changes in light are followed by GI Response. Needs the GI denoiser. No extra cost.
value.GI_HISTORY_MAX.8=8 frames (fast, noisy)
value.GI_HISTORY_MAX.16=16 frames
value.GI_HISTORY_MAX.32=32 frames
value.GI_HISTORY_MAX.64=64 frames (clean)
value.GI_HISTORY_MAX.128=128 frames (experimental, GI drifts a little darker)
option.GI_RESPONSE_STRENGTH=GI Response
option.GI_RESPONSE_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the GI history is cut when the lighting changes. Higher catches up sooner after placing or breaking a light, with a little more flicker. Needs the GI denoiser. No extra cost.
option.GI_SHORT_HISTORY=GI Wide Blur for New Areas
option.GI_SHORT_HISTORY.comment=Where the GI history is shorter than this (just turned into view, uncovered, or the light just changed), GI is blurred twice as wide with the same number of taps, so the blotches calm down sooner. Needs the GI denoiser. No extra cost.
value.GI_SHORT_HISTORY.0=Off
value.GI_SHORT_HISTORY.4=4 frames
value.GI_SHORT_HISTORY.8=8 frames
value.GI_SHORT_HISTORY.16=16 frames
option.GI_VOXEL_FADE=Voxel GI Fade Distance
option.GI_VOXEL_FADE.comment=Width in blocks over which voxel ray traced GI fades into the plain sky light at the edge of the voxel range. Wider hides the edge better when flying down from the sky or looking at distant terrain. Voxel ray tracing only.
option.GI_HIT_REUSE=Reuse Light at GI Hits
option.GI_HIT_REUSE.comment=When a GI ray hits a surface that is on screen, its placed-light lighting is taken from the direct lighting result instead of summing the lights again. Faster where there are many lights. The bounce color leans slightly toward the color of nearby lights. SSGI and voxel ray tracing only.
option.GI_HIT_LIGHTS=Lights at Off-screen GI Hits
option.GI_HIT_LIGHTS.comment=Most placed lights summed when a GI ray hits a surface off screen. Where there are many lights, they are taken at even steps in brightness order and scaled by the ratio. Lower is faster where there are many lights, with a little more noise in light bounced from off screen. SSGI and voxel ray tracing only.
value.GI_HIT_LIGHTS.0=All

# Reflector light
screen.REFLECTOR_OPTIONS=Reflector Light
option.REFLECTOR_LIGHT=Reflector Light
option.REFLECTOR_LIGHT.comment=Glass, ice, metal and mineral blocks (lapis, emerald, diamond, gold) bounce sun, moon and block light onto their surroundings. A bright patch shaped like the window falls on the ground next to it, and a metal wall tints the area around it. Computed in the GI pass, so it has no effect when both GI and AO are off. It only looks for flat faces along the axes and traces one ray at the face it finds, but the GI pass gets a little heavier.
option.REFLECTOR_SUN=Sun & Moon Reflection
option.REFLECTOR_SUN.comment=Reflected sun and moon light. It arrives in the direction set by the face and the light, as a patch the shape of the face that does not fade with distance.
option.REFLECTOR_BLOCKLIGHT=Block Light Reflection
option.REFLECTOR_BLOCKLIGHT.comment=Reflected block light. Lights the surroundings as if the light sat at its mirror image behind the reflecting face. Visible at night, in caves and indoors near windows and metal walls, and barely visible under a daytime sky.
option.REFLECTOR_STRENGTH=Reflection Strength
option.REFLECTOR_STRENGTH.comment=Overall multiplier of the reflected light. 1 is the material reflectance. A pane of glass reflects about 8% (more at grazing angles), so the default 1.5 and the per-material multipliers make the reflection clearly visible. Lower them for a subtler look.
option.REFLECTOR_GLASS_STRENGTH=Glass & Ice Reflection
option.REFLECTOR_GLASS_STRENGTH.comment=Multiplier for light reflected by glass, stained glass, glass panes and ice. Stained glass tints it.
option.REFLECTOR_METAL_STRENGTH=Metal Reflection
option.REFLECTOR_METAL_STRENGTH.comment=Multiplier for the mirror reflection of metal blocks (iron, copper, gold...). GI already returns their diffuse bounce in the block color, so this only adds the mirror part. Lower it if metal walls look too bright.
option.REFLECTOR_GEM_STRENGTH=Mineral Reflection
option.REFLECTOR_GEM_STRENGTH.comment=Multiplier for the reflection of lapis, emerald and diamond blocks. The reflection carries the block color.
option.REFLECTOR_GEM_PATTERN=Mineral Light Pattern
option.REFLECTOR_GEM_PATTERN.comment=Lapis, emerald and diamond blocks have a bumpy face, so light reflects in slightly different directions from place to place and gathers in some spots and scatters in others on the surface it lands on. The bumps come from the block texture's brightness. The farther the surface, the larger and blurrier the pattern.
option.REFLECTOR_GEM_PATTERN_STRENGTH=Mineral Pattern Strength
option.REFLECTOR_GEM_PATTERN_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the mineral pattern shows. Higher gives brighter and darker spots.
option.REFLECTOR_METAL_PATTERN=Metal Light Pattern
option.REFLECTOR_METAL_PATTERN.comment=The same pattern for metal blocks (iron, gold...). Metal faces are smoother and their reflection is wider, so the pattern is gentler and blurs out sooner.
option.REFLECTOR_METAL_PATTERN_STRENGTH=Metal Pattern Strength
option.REFLECTOR_METAL_PATTERN_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the metal pattern shows.
option.REFLECTOR_DISTANCE=Sun Reflection Distance
option.REFLECTOR_DISTANCE.comment=How far to look for reflected sun and moon light (blocks). At a sun height of 45 degrees the light lands as far from the wall as the window is high. Longer shows reflections of taller buildings but costs more.
option.REFLECTOR_BLOCKLIGHT_COUNT=Reflected Lights
option.REFLECTOR_BLOCKLIGHT_COUNT.comment=How many lights get their reflection computed (brightest first in the lit point's bin). More adds reflections where there are many lights but costs more.
option.REFLECTOR_GLINT=Metal & Mineral Glints
option.REFLECTOR_GLINT.comment=Splits the faces of metal and mineral blocks (polished stone included) into 1/16 block facets and lights only the facets that catch the image of the sun or a lamp. Lit points change as you walk. The average highlight is unchanged. Fades out where a texel gets smaller than a pixel.
option.REFLECTOR_GLINT_STRENGTH=Glint Strength
option.REFLECTOR_GLINT_STRENGTH.comment=How far the facets tilt. Higher gives fewer, brighter points; 0 is the plain highlight.

# Materials
option.PBR_FORMAT=PBR Format
value.PBR_FORMAT.0=None
value.PBR_FORMAT.1=labPBR
option.NORMAL_MAPPING=Normal Mapping
option.GENERATED_NORMALS=Generated Normals
option.GENERATED_NORMALS.comment=Builds normals from the texture when no PBR resource pack is used.
option.GENERATED_NORMAL_STRENGTH=Generated Normal Strength
option.GENERATED_NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the generated bumps. Independent of texture resolution; 1 is the strength for a 16 texels per block picture. Higher makes bumps clearer, including under a noon sun and next to light sources, but fine patterns get grainy when too high, and metal or glossy surfaces may show diagonal stripes.
option.GENERATED_NORMAL_ENTITIES=Generated Normals on Entities
option.GENERATED_NORMAL_ENTITIES.comment=Also builds normals for mobs, armor, held items and dropped items, so large flat surfaces show bumps in the light. No effect when Generated Normals is off.
option.AUTO_METAL_PARTS=Metal Parts
option.AUTO_METAL_PARTS.comment=Makes only the metal pixels of partly metal blocks (rails, iron bars, chains, lantern frames, hoppers, cauldrons, copper doors) and of metal tools and armor shine like metal blocks. Wood and flames stay non-metal. Not used for textures that have a PBR specular map.
option.ALBEDO_CONCRETE_STRENGTH=Concrete Reflectance
option.ALBEDO_CONCRETE_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of concrete and concrete powder colors. Higher values make both the blocks and their bounce light brighter while keeping the color strength, for a strong painted look. 1 = the vanilla texture color.
option.ALBEDO_WOOL_STRENGTH=Wool, Carpet and Bed Reflectance
option.ALBEDO_WOOL_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of wool, carpet and bed colors (the whole bed, including the pillow and the wooden frame). Higher values make both the blocks and their bounce light brighter while keeping the color strength. 1 = the vanilla texture color.
option.ALBEDO_TERRACOTTA_STRENGTH=Terracotta and Glazed Terracotta Reflectance
option.ALBEDO_TERRACOTTA_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of terracotta and glazed terracotta colors. Higher values make both the blocks and their bounce light brighter and deeper. The whole block is scaled by the same amount so glazed patterns keep their contrast; bright patterns that cannot get brighter get more saturated instead. 1 = the vanilla texture color.
option.ALBEDO_DYED_STRENGTH=Banner, Candle and Shulker Box Reflectance
option.ALBEDO_DYED_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of banner, unlit candle and shulker box colors. Higher values make both the blocks and their bounce light brighter while keeping the color strength. 1 = the vanilla texture color.
option.POM=Parallax Occlusion Mapping
option.POM_DEPTH=POM Depth
option.POM_SAMPLES=POM Samples
option.POM_SHADOW=POM Self Shadows
option.SSS=Subsurface Scattering
option.SSS.comment=Sunlight, moonlight and hand-held light shine through leaves, grass, snow and player skin when lit from behind, and shadows on these surfaces soften slightly. Adds a few shadow map samples on these surfaces.
option.SSS_STRENGTH=Subsurface Scattering Strength
option.SSS_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the sunlight and moonlight shining through these surfaces. No effect when Subsurface Scattering is off.
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.WAVING_LEAVES=Waving Leaves
option.RAIN_PUDDLES=Rain Puddles
option.RAIN_WETNESS=Wetness
option.RAIN_WETNESS.comment=How dark and glossy the ground gets in the rain
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=Puddle Amount
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT.comment=Share of the ground covered by puddles after a long rain (0.3 = 30%)
option.PUDDLE_SIZE=Puddle Size
option.PUDDLE_SIZE.comment=At 1.0 a puddle spans about 2-10 blocks
option.PUDDLE_RIPPLES=Puddle Ripples
option.PUDDLE_RIPPLES.comment=Strength of the raindrop ripples on puddles
option.RAIN_WET_HALFLIFE=Wetting Time
option.RAIN_WET_HALFLIFE.comment=Seconds after rain starts until the ground is half wet. Rain clouds and fog build up at the same pace
suffix.RAIN_WET_HALFLIFE= s
option.RAIN_DRY_HALFLIFE=Drying Time
option.RAIN_DRY_HALFLIFE.comment=Seconds after rain stops until the ground is half dry. Puddles, rain clouds and fog clear at the same pace
suffix.RAIN_DRY_HALFLIFE= s
option.EMISSION_GLARE=Light Source Glare
option.EMISSION_GLARE.comment=Makes the glowing parts of torches, lanterns, fire and other light sources 4x brighter so their cores blow out to white, and keeps the part above white as fine sparkle that reaches bloom and lens effects. Looks like a light photographed directly, but is very eye-catching
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH=Emission Strength
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the glowing parts of torches, lanterns and other light sources. Higher values blow out the core
option.EMISSION_TORCH_BRIGHTNESS=Torch Brightness
option.EMISSION_TORCH_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright the glowing part of torches (soul, redstone and copper included) looks on screen. Does not change the light they cast
option.EMISSION_FIRE_BRIGHTNESS=Fire Brightness
option.EMISSION_FIRE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright fire, soul fire, campfires and candles look on screen. Does not change the light they cast
option.EMISSION_LANTERN_BRIGHTNESS=Lantern Brightness
option.EMISSION_LANTERN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright the glowing part of lanterns (soul and copper included) looks on screen. Lower values show more of the texture pattern. Does not change the light they cast
option.EMISSION_BLOCK_BRIGHTNESS=Light Block Brightness
option.EMISSION_BLOCK_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright blocks that glow as a whole (glowstone, sea lantern, redstone lamp, jack o'lantern, froglights, shroomlight) look on screen. Lower values show more of the texture pattern. Does not change the light they cast
option.EMISSION_BEACON_BRIGHTNESS=Beacon Brightness
option.EMISSION_BEACON_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright the beacon block and its beam look on screen. The beam is always visible from far away, so a low value keeps it from standing out. Does not change the light the beacon casts
option.EMISSION_BEACON_SCATTER=Beacon Beam Scattering
option.EMISSION_BEACON_SCATTER.comment=Draws the beam as light scattered by the air. It gets brighter when you look down along it from above or along its length, and stronger with a glow around it in fog, haze and rain. Faint against the daytime sky, clear at night. OFF = a thin line of constant brightness. No cost when no beam is on screen
option.EMISSION_BEACON_SCATTER_STRENGTH=Beacon Beam Glow
option.EMISSION_BEACON_SCATTER_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly fog, haze and rain around the beam light up and glow. 0 = no glow
option.EMISSION_CHARGED_CREEPER_BRIGHTNESS=Charged Creeper / Wither Armor Brightness
option.EMISSION_CHARGED_CREEPER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How brightly the electric swirl of a creeper charged by lightning and of the wither's armor glows blue-white, so it stands out at night. 0 = vanilla brightness. Does not change the light it casts
option.CREAKING_EYE_BRIGHTNESS=Creaking Eye Brightness
option.CREAKING_EYE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How brightly the glowing eyes of a creaking shine in eerie orange-red. 0 = no glow. Does not cast light on the surroundings
option.GLOW_LICHEN_LIGHT=Glow Lichen Light
option.GLOW_LICHEN_LIGHT.comment=Makes glow lichen a light source that lights its surroundings. When off, only the glowing look remains.
option.GLOW_LICHEN_BRIGHTNESS=Glow Lichen Light Strength
option.GLOW_LICHEN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How strongly glow lichen lights its surroundings. Higher values light farther.
option.FIREFLY_BUSH_BRIGHTNESS=Firefly Bush Light Strength
option.FIREFLY_BUSH_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How strongly firefly bushes light their surroundings. Higher values light farther.
option.EYEBLOSSOM_BRIGHTNESS=Open Eyeblossom Brightness
option.EYEBLOSSOM_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How brightly open eyeblossoms glow pale orange at night, and how strongly they softly light their surroundings. 0 = no glow.
option.LAVA_BRIGHTNESS=Lava Brightness
option.LAVA_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright lava itself looks on screen. Up to 1 it gets brighter while staying deep orange; above 1 it shifts toward a bright, pale orange, and at 5 it is about as bright as the brightest glow it casts on the rock next to it. Lower values give a darker, deeper orange. Does not change the light it casts. 0 = no extra brightening (darker orange)
option.LAVA_BLOOM=Lava Bloom
option.LAVA_BLOOM.comment=Strength of the glow around lava. 0 = same bloom as other objects
option.LAVA_LIGHT=Lava Light
option.LAVA_LIGHT.comment=Strength of the light lava casts on the surrounding terrain. Lava itself can look slightly brighter from the light it receives back. 0 = lava lights nothing
option.FIREWORK_GLOW=Firework Glow
option.FIREWORK_GLOW.comment=Self-lit particles such as firework sparks (also end rod and totem particles) glow brightly in their own color and spread through bloom, as does the flash when a firework bursts. Small distant sparks stay visible. OFF = lit by the surroundings like other particles
option.FIREWORK_GLOW_STRENGTH=Firework Glow Brightness
option.FIREWORK_GLOW_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of glowing particles. Higher = larger white core and wider glow
option.FIREWORK_TWINKLE_STRENGTH=Firework Twinkle
option.FIREWORK_TWINKLE_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness flicker of glowing particles. Nearby sparks twinkle slightly out of step. 0 = steady
option.FIREWORK_LIGHT=Firework Light
option.FIREWORK_LIGHT.comment=When a firework bursts, it lights the ground and walls under the open sky and the surrounding air (fog, smoke) in its color, and shows on water, glass and wet ground. Walls and hills cast shadows (with light source shadows)
option.FIREWORK_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Firework Light Strength
option.FIREWORK_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the light fireworks cast on their surroundings. Does not change the brightness of the sparks
option.GENERIC_LIGHT=Unlisted Emissive Block Light
option.GENERIC_LIGHT.comment=Blocks that give off light but are not listed in this pack (such as modded blocks) become light sources from the light level the game reports for them, light their surroundings and glow in their bright parts. Listed blocks are unchanged. Nothing happens for blocks below light level 2, or where the light level is not available (old Iris)
option.GENERIC_LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Unlisted Emissive Block Light Strength
option.GENERIC_LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How strongly unlisted emissive blocks light their surroundings. Higher values light farther. 0 = they do not light their surroundings. Scales with the block's light level
option.GENERIC_LIGHT_COLOR=Unlisted Emissive Block Light Color
option.GENERIC_LIGHT_COLOR.comment=The game does not report block colors, so the light uses a single color. Fire: follows the block light warmth. White: no tint. Cool White: a cold white
value.GENERIC_LIGHT_COLOR.0=Fire
value.GENERIC_LIGHT_COLOR.1=White
value.GENERIC_LIGHT_COLOR.2=Cool White

# Water & reflections
option.WATER_WAVES=Water Waves
option.WATER_WAVE_HEIGHT=Wave Height
screen.WATER_WAVE_OPTIONS=Wave Options (All Water)
screen.WATER_KIND_OPTIONS=Sea / Lake / River
screen.WATER_KIND_OPTIONS.comment=Water settings for each kind of water, in columns: sea, lake, river. The biome the camera is in picks the kind (ocean biomes are sea, river biomes are river, everything else is lake) and changes it smoothly over a few seconds
screen.WATER_GLINT_OPTIONS=Glitter & Reflection Bloom
option.WATER_WAVE_HEIGHT.comment=Multiplier on the wave height given by the wind speed. Applies to all water, on top of the sea / lake / river wave height
option.WATER_WAVE_LENGTH=Wavelength Scale
option.WATER_WAVE_LENGTH.comment=Scales the size of every wave
option.WATER_WIND_SPEED=Sea Wind Speed
option.WATER_WIND_SPEED.comment=Wind over the ocean in m/s. Stronger wind makes longer, higher waves and whitecaps. Lake and river wind are set relative to this
option.WATER_CHOPPINESS=Choppiness
option.WATER_CHOPPINESS.comment=Sharpens the wave crests and flattens the troughs. Applies to all water, on top of the sea / lake / river choppiness
option.WATER_SEA_WAVE_HEIGHT=Sea Wave Height
option.WATER_SEA_WAVE_HEIGHT.comment=Multiplier on the height of sea waves. 0: flat
option.WATER_LAKE_WAVE_HEIGHT=Lake Wave Height
option.WATER_LAKE_WAVE_HEIGHT.comment=Multiplier on the height of waves on lakes and ponds. 0: flat
option.WATER_RIVER_WAVE_HEIGHT=River Wave Height
option.WATER_RIVER_WAVE_HEIGHT.comment=Multiplier on the height of river waves. 0: flat
option.WATER_SEA_CHOPPINESS=Sea Choppiness
option.WATER_SEA_CHOPPINESS.comment=Multiplier on how sharp the sea wave crests are
option.WATER_LAKE_CHOPPINESS=Lake Choppiness
option.WATER_LAKE_CHOPPINESS.comment=Multiplier on how sharp the lake wave crests are
option.WATER_RIVER_CHOPPINESS=River Choppiness
option.WATER_RIVER_CHOPPINESS.comment=Multiplier on how sharp the river wave crests are
option.WATER_LAKE_REFLECT_SCATTER=Lake Reflection Blur
option.WATER_LAKE_REFLECT_SCATTER.comment=How much waves smaller than a pixel blur reflections on lakes and ponds. 0: a mirror, so the far shore shows up sharp even when zoomed in. Needs Reflections set to SSR + Rough or higher
option.WATER_RIVER_REFLECT_SCATTER=River Reflection Blur
option.WATER_RIVER_REFLECT_SCATTER.comment=How much waves smaller than a pixel blur reflections on rivers. 0: a mirror. Needs Reflections set to SSR + Rough or higher
option.WATER_LAKE_TYPE=Lake Water Color
value.WATER_LAKE_TYPE.0=Open Ocean (Blue)
value.WATER_LAKE_TYPE.1=Coastal (Green)
value.WATER_LAKE_TYPE.2=Clear
option.WATER_LAKE_TYPE.comment=Absorption and scattering of lake water. Affects both the view through the surface and the underwater fog
option.WATER_RIVER_TYPE=River Water Color
value.WATER_RIVER_TYPE.0=Open Ocean (Blue)
value.WATER_RIVER_TYPE.1=Coastal (Green)
value.WATER_RIVER_TYPE.2=Clear
option.WATER_RIVER_TYPE.comment=Absorption and scattering of river water. Affects both the view through the surface and the underwater fog
option.WATER_SEA_ABSORPTION=Sea Depth Tint
option.WATER_SEA_ABSORPTION.comment=Multiplier on light absorption in sea water. Higher: deep water turns dark and colored sooner and the bottom fades faster. Lower: clearer water you can see deeper into
option.WATER_LAKE_ABSORPTION=Lake Depth Tint
option.WATER_LAKE_ABSORPTION.comment=Multiplier on light absorption in lake water. Higher: deep water turns dark and colored sooner. Lower: clearer water
option.WATER_RIVER_ABSORPTION=River Depth Tint
option.WATER_RIVER_ABSORPTION.comment=Multiplier on light absorption in river water. Higher: deep water turns dark and colored sooner. Lower: clearer water
option.WATER_SEA_TURBIDITY=Sea Turbidity
option.WATER_SEA_TURBIDITY.comment=Multiplier on light scattering in sea water. Higher: milkier water that hides the bottom and glows with the water color. 0: no haze, only absorption
option.WATER_LAKE_TURBIDITY=Lake Turbidity
option.WATER_LAKE_TURBIDITY.comment=Multiplier on light scattering in lake water. Higher: milkier water that hides the bottom. 0: no haze, only absorption
option.WATER_RIVER_TURBIDITY=River Turbidity
option.WATER_RIVER_TURBIDITY.comment=Multiplier on light scattering in river water. Higher: milkier water that hides the bottom. 0: no haze, only absorption
option.WATER_RIPPLES=Ripples
option.WATER_RIPPLES.comment=Strength of the short waves (under 1 block)
option.WATER_FOAM=Foam
option.WATER_FOAM.comment=Whitecaps on breaking crests offshore. More with stronger wind. Not shown at the shoreline
option.WATER_LAKE_WAVES=Lake Wind
option.WATER_LAKE_WAVES.comment=Wind on lakes and ponds relative to the sea. Lakes also have a short fetch, so their waves stay small
option.WATER_RIVER_WAVES=River Wind
option.WATER_RIVER_WAVES.comment=Wind on rivers relative to the sea. Sloped flowing water also moves downstream
option.WATER_GLITTER=Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER.comment=Draws the sun and moon mirrored by ripples smaller than a pixel as bright points that drift with the waves and thin out toward the edge of the path. Overall brightness stays about the same. Off keeps a smooth reflection. Slightly heavier
option.WATER_GLITTER_DENSITY=Glitter Amount
option.WATER_GLITTER_DENSITY.comment=Number of glitter points on the water. Higher: more, finer points packed close together. Lower: fewer, brighter points spread apart. Overall brightness stays the same. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_NIGHT_DENSITY=Night Glitter Amount
option.WATER_GLITTER_NIGHT_DENSITY.comment=Multiplier on the glitter amount while the moon is the light source. The moon path is far dimmer than the sun path, so lowering this leaves fewer points and gathers the same brightness into sparse white points. Overall brightness stays the same. Daytime is unchanged. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_LENGTH=Glitter Length
option.WATER_GLITTER_LENGTH.comment=Length of the horizontal streaks that glitter points form. Higher: longer streaks. Lower: shorter, rounder lumps. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_SINGLE=Round Glitter
option.WATER_GLITTER_SINGLE.comment=Share of the brightest points that stay one round point instead of splitting into a horizontal streak. 0: every point is a streak. Higher: more round points. Needs Water Glitter
option.WATER_REFLECT_SCATTER=Sea Reflection Blur
option.WATER_REFLECT_SCATTER.comment=How much waves smaller than a pixel blur the reflection of objects and sky on the sea. 0: a perfect mirror. Higher: reflections of distant trees and ice smear vertically and melt into the sky color. Calm water and water close to the camera stay mirrors. Needs Reflections set to SSR + Rough or higher
option.WATER_PARALLAX=Water Parallax
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Water Refraction
value.WATER_REFRACTION.0=Off
value.WATER_REFRACTION.1=Screen Space
value.WATER_REFRACTION.2=Ray Traced
option.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE=Refraction Method
option.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.comment=Refraction of water seen from above. Waves Only: only the bending caused by waves (the bottom appears at its real depth; cheap). Edge Fade: full refraction, weakened toward the screen edges (the bottom slides near the edges). Voxel Traced: full refraction, and parts of the bottom that are not on screen are traced through voxels (the bottom looks shallower, like real water; off-screen parts use an approximate untextured color)
value.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.0=Waves Only
value.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.1=Edge Fade
value.WATER_REFRACTION_MODE.2=Voxel Traced
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Water Caustics
option.WATER_TEXTURE=Vanilla Water Texture
option.WATER_FOG_DENSITY=Water Fog Density
option.WATER_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Multiplier on absorption and scattering of all water, on top of the sea / lake / river depth tint and turbidity. Affects both the view through the surface and the underwater fog
option.WATER_TYPE=Sea Water Color
value.WATER_TYPE.0=Open Ocean (Blue)
value.WATER_TYPE.1=Coastal (Green)
value.WATER_TYPE.2=Clear
option.WATER_TYPE.comment=Absorption and scattering of sea water. Affects both the view through the surface and the underwater fog
option.REFLECTIONS=Reflections
value.REFLECTIONS.0=Sky Only
value.REFLECTIONS.1=SSR
value.REFLECTIONS.2=SSR + Rough
value.REFLECTIONS.3=SSR + Voxel
option.SSR_STEPS=Reflection Steps
option.REFLECTION_FILTER_STRENGTH=Rough Reflection Smoothing
value.REFLECTION_FILTER_STRENGTH.0=Off
value.REFLECTION_FILTER_STRENGTH.1=Low
value.REFLECTION_FILTER_STRENGTH.2=Medium
value.REFLECTION_FILTER_STRENGTH.3=High
option.REFLECTION_FILTER_STRENGTH.comment=Smooths the grain and bright dots in reflections on metal and glossy stone by blending with nearby texels of the same surface. Higher is calmer with slightly blurrier reflections. Off is cheaper
option.SPECULAR_SUN_STRENGTH=Sun Reflection Strength
option.SPECULAR_SUN_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the daytime sun reflected on water, puddles, glass and metal. 1 is the true mirror image of the sun disc, 0 shows no reflection
option.SPECULAR_MOON_STRENGTH=Moon Reflection Strength
option.SPECULAR_MOON_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the moon (and the End light) reflected at night. 1 is the true mirror image of the moon disc drawn in the sky, 0 shows no reflection. Higher values brighten the glint on rough surfaces such as iron blocks and stone, and the moon path on wavy water (only the center of a mirror-smooth surface never gets brighter than the disc)
option.SPECULAR_BLOCK_STRENGTH=Light Source Reflection Strength
option.SPECULAR_BLOCK_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of placed, held and item light sources reflected on surfaces. 1 is the true mirror image of the light, 0 shows no reflection
option.SPECULAR_SPARKLE=Reflection Sparkle
option.SPECULAR_SPARKLE.comment=Keeps the blown-out part of sun and light reflections on water, glass and metal intact so bloom and lens effects pick it up. Off lets anti-aliasing weaken small highlights

# Sky
option.ATMOSPHERE_MODE=Atmosphere
value.ATMOSPHERE_MODE.0=Analytic
value.ATMOSPHERE_MODE.1=Physical (LUT)
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Brightness
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS=Moon Brightness
option.SKY_BRIGHTNESS=Sky Brightness
option.SKY_AMBIENT_SATURATION=Sky Ambient Saturation
option.SKY_AMBIENT_SATURATION.comment=How colorful the sky light that fills the shade is. Higher values make shade bluer against the warm sunlight. 0.3 = a subtle tint, 1 = the full sky color (shaded snow turns quite blue). Multiplies the Look preset value (1 with Natural)
option.SUN_MOON_STYLE=Sun & Moon
option.SUN_MOON_STYLE.comment=Vanilla = the game's sun and moon textures. Round = a round sun and a plain round moon that shows only the phase. Real Moon = a round sun and the moon drawn from NASA photographs of each phase (maria and craters). The moon's brightness, glint on water, flare and cloud shadows are the same as Round
value.SUN_MOON_STYLE.0=Vanilla
value.SUN_MOON_STYLE.1=Round
value.SUN_MOON_STYLE.2=Real Moon
option.STARS=Stars
option.TWILIGHT_STRETCH=Twilight Length
option.TWILIGHT_STRETCH.comment=Makes the colors of dawn and dusk last longer by compressing how far the sun sinks below the horizon, for the sky only. Civil twilight lasts about 20 seconds in Minecraft. 1 = real length. The sun disk, sunlight and shadows are unchanged

# Clouds
option.CLOUDS=Clouds
value.CLOUDS.0=Off
value.CLOUDS.1=Vanilla
value.CLOUDS.2=Volumetric 2D
value.CLOUDS.3=Volumetric 3D
option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud Quality
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=Ray march step counts. The shape and shading of the clouds are the same at every level; higher levels have less noise and cost more
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.0=Low
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.1=Medium
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.2=High
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.3=Ultra
option.CLOUD_RES=Cloud Resolution
value.CLOUD_RES.1=Full
value.CLOUD_RES.2=Half
value.CLOUD_RES.4=Quarter
option.CLOUD_TEMPORAL=Temporal Upscaling
option.CLOUD_MOTION=Cloud Motion Handling
option.CLOUD_MOTION.comment=How clouds are drawn while the camera moves or is inside a cloud. Classic accumulates history the same way as when standing still (leaves ghosts). Auto weakens the history where the camera's parallax would misplace it (no ghosts, still look unchanged). Always weak never trusts the history (no ghosts, noisier)
value.CLOUD_MOTION.0=Classic
value.CLOUD_MOTION.1=Auto
value.CLOUD_MOTION.2=Always weak
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=Multiplier for all cloud layers. The actual amount also changes with the daily weather, time of day and rain
option.CLOUD_SCALE=Cloud Scale
option.CLOUD_SCALE.comment=Horizontal size multiplier for all clouds, shared by every height template
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET=Cloud Height Template
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.comment=Maps real cloud heights onto the world. Vanilla: cumulus base y 165, cumulonimbus tops and cirrus near y 280-300. Tall World: base y 525, tops near y 1800. Realistic: 1 block = 1 m (base 1500, cirrus 8-10 km). Custom: the altitude and thickness sliders in each layer screen. Upper layers are compressed more than low clouds so cumulus keep a natural shape
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.0=Vanilla (-64 to 320)
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.1=Tall World (~2000)
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.2=Realistic (1 block = 1 m)
value.CLOUD_HEIGHT_PRESET.3=Custom
option.CLOUD_STYLE=Cloud Style
option.CLOUD_STYLE.comment=Picks the shape, density and lighting of the low clouds and the fair-weather amount of each layer. The cloud settings below multiply the style's values. Rain and thunderstorm clouds look nearly the same in every style except Vanilla Shape. Ray: lobed cumulus with blue sky between clumps. Bliss-like: smaller scattered clumps with frayed edges and deep shading. Vanilla Shape: flat slab clouds of uniform thickness with slightly rounded corners at the vanilla cloud height, pattern (vanilla or resource pack cloud texture) and drift, on a grid twice the vanilla 12 blocks (24). Mid and high clouds, cirrus and cumulonimbus are not drawn, and cloud amount, size, wind and height template do not change them. In rain and thunderstorms the gaps fill with cloud until the sky is almost covered, and the clouds darken and thicken. They are lighter than the Ray style. Realistic: density close to measured cumulus, crisp outlines. Cotton Candy: soft round clouds with a wide hazy edge. Towering Cumulus: tall white cumulus standing apart. Sparse Fair-Weather: small flat cumulus scattered over a wide blue sky. Stratocumulus Overcast: flat clumps covering most of the sky. Custom: set in "Custom Cloud Style"
value.CLOUD_STYLE.0=Custom
value.CLOUD_STYLE.1=Ray
value.CLOUD_STYLE.2=Bliss-like
value.CLOUD_STYLE.3=Vanilla Shape
value.CLOUD_STYLE.4=Realistic
value.CLOUD_STYLE.5=Cotton Candy
value.CLOUD_STYLE.6=Towering Cumulus
value.CLOUD_STYLE.7=Sparse Fair-Weather
value.CLOUD_STYLE.8=Stratocumulus Overcast
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_THICKNESS=Thickness
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_THICKNESS.comment=Thickness in blocks of the vanilla-shaped cloud slab, the same for every cell. The base stays at the vanilla cloud height and the cloud grows upward. A thicker cloud shows clearer side faces and a shaded base from below
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT=Upper Tiers
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.0=None
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.1=Middle
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.2=Middle and High
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COUNT.comment=Stacks tiers of blocky clouds above the vanilla-shaped clouds, made from the same pattern turned, shifted and thinned. Middle: a thin layer of scaly grains. High: a layer of long thin streaks. Each tier drifts in its own direction and speed, and is hidden from below a rain deck. Costs about 0.5 ms with both tiers
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COVERAGE=Upper Tier Coverage
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_COVERAGE.comment=Share of the pattern cells kept in the upper tiers. Lower values leave sparser grains. The high tier keeps 0.8 times the middle tier's share
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT=Upper Tier Height
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT.0=High
value.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT.1=Below Build Limit
option.CLOUD_VANILLA_TIER_HEIGHT.comment=High: the middle tier is about 190 blocks and the high tier about 410 blocks above the clouds, so the tiers stand far apart and give depth. Below Build Limit: about 70 and 120 blocks above, so you can fly up between the tiers. Thunderstorm towers and anvils are lowered to match
option.CLOUD_S_SHAPE=Shape
option.CLOUD_S_SHAPE.comment=Cumulus: 3D clouds built from stacked lobes. Vanilla Shape: soft volumetric clouds placed like the vanilla clouds (in fair weather about 10% of the Ray style cost)
value.CLOUD_S_SHAPE.0=Cumulus
value.CLOUD_S_SHAPE.1=Vanilla Shape
option.CLOUD_S_HEIGHT=Cumulus Height
option.CLOUD_S_HEIGHT.comment=Multiplier for how tall cumulus grow. Higher gives towering cumulus, lower gives flat fair-weather cumulus
option.CLOUD_S_CONVECTION=Convection
option.CLOUD_S_CONVECTION.comment=Higher lets cumulus develop more and spread into stratocumulus less
option.CLOUD_S_TYPE_SHIFT=Cloud Type Shift
option.CLOUD_S_TYPE_SHIFT.comment=Shifts fair-weather clouds toward stratocumulus (negative) or cumulus (positive)
option.CLOUD_S_SPACING=Cloud Spacing
option.CLOUD_S_SPACING.comment=Size of the clear gap around large clouds. Higher removes small clouds and opens space between clumps
option.CLOUD_S_LOBES=Lobes
option.CLOUD_S_LOBES.comment=Depth of the lobes carved into the cloud surface. 0 gives smooth round clumps
option.CLOUD_S_BASE_RAGGED=Ragged Base
option.CLOUD_S_BASE_RAGGED.comment=Size of the bumps on the cloud base. 0 gives a flat base
option.CLOUD_S_LOBE_SHADE=Lobe Shading
option.CLOUD_S_LOBE_SHADE.comment=Depth of the shadow under each lobe. Higher increases the contrast between sunlit and shaded lobes
option.CLOUD_S_MULTISCATTER=Sunlit Brightness
option.CLOUD_S_MULTISCATTER.comment=Multiplier for light scattered many times inside the cloud. Higher makes the sunlit side whiter and the shaded side brighter
option.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET=Cloud Climate
option.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.comment=Which cloud types appear and how often, with day-to-day changes. Temperate: cumulus and cirrus, stratocumulus on humid days. Tropical: afternoon towering cumulus and distant cumulonimbus. Arid: few small clouds. Polar: low stratus decks and ice clouds. Maritime: wide stratocumulus and puffy cumulus. Custom: the Climate sliders in each layer screen
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.0=Temperate
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.1=Tropical
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.2=Arid
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.3=Polar
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.4=Maritime
value.CLOUD_REGION_PRESET.5=Custom
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE=Low Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the low cloud base
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS=Low Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=Custom height template only. Blocks for the cumulus layer (real 4.5 km). Also sets the scale of every layer left on automatic
option.CLOUD_C_LOW=Climate: Low Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_C_LOW.comment=Custom climate only. Average low cloud cover (varies by day)
option.CLOUD_C_CONVECTION=Climate: Convection
option.CLOUD_C_CONVECTION.comment=Custom climate only. How tall cumulus grow on sunny afternoons
option.CLOUD_C_STRATUS=Climate: Stratocumulus
option.CLOUD_C_STRATUS.comment=Custom climate only. How often clouds spread into flat layers on humid days and at night
option.CLOUD_C_MID=Climate: Mid Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_C_HIGH=Climate: High Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_C_STORMS=Climate: Fair Weather Storms
option.CLOUD_C_STORMS.comment=Custom climate only. Chance of distant cumulonimbus on unstable afternoons (thunderstorms always make them)
option.CLOUD_CUMULONIMBUS=Cumulonimbus
option.CLOUD_CUMULONIMBUS.comment=Thunderstorm towers with anvils, overshooting tops, mammatus and rain shafts. Not drawn by the vanilla-shaped clouds. Only costs while storms exist
option.CLOUD_SPEED=Cloud Speed
option.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER=Multiple Scattering Octaves
option.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER.comment=How many octaves the multiple scattering is split into. With fewer octaves the rest is folded into the last one, so the brightness stays about the same; more octaves cost more
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS=High Clouds
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS.comment=Thin translucent ice clouds around 9 km: cirrus tufts with sheared fall streaks, cirrocumulus ripples and cirrostratus veils (faint 22 degree halo)
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS_COVERAGE=High Cloud Amount
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadows
option.CLOUD_INTERIOR_VISIBILITY=Visibility Inside Clouds
option.CLOUD_INTERIOR_VISIBILITY.comment=How far you can see while inside a cloud, in blocks (a smaller value is thicker). At the default of 64 the inside of a cloud is drawn with the same density and light as seen from outside (thin at the edges, dense in the core, clear in the gaps); smaller values thicken the cloud near the camera, fading in smoothly as you enter. The visibility also scales with the cloud density setting (Low Cloud Density). Vanilla-shaped clouds get a fog inside the slab that veils things at this distance down to 5% at the default density, and sight lines that leave through the top or bottom of the slab are not veiled beyond that point. 0 turns off every inside-cloud effect, including hiding an off-screen sun or moon behind the cloud for lens flares and god rays
option.CLOUD_LOW_COVERAGE=Low Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_LOW_COVERAGE.comment=Multiplier on the amount of cumulus, stratocumulus and rain clouds, on top of Cloud Coverage and the climate
option.CLOUD_LOW_DENSITY=Low Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_LOW_DENSITY.comment=Optical density of low clouds. The default 0.25 gives soft clouds with translucent edges, higher values give denser, more solid clouds. Rain and storm clouds scale with it. Shading (lit side and dark base) is kept at low values
option.CLOUD_LOW_SCALE=Low Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_LOW_SCALE.comment=Horizontal size multiplier for low clouds only (on top of Cloud Scale)
option.CLOUD_LOW_EROSION=Low Cloud Erosion
option.CLOUD_LOW_EROSION.comment=How strongly billows and wisps cut into the edges. Lower gives smooth cotton, higher gives cauliflower tops and ragged bases
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND=Low Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND.comment=m/s at the low cloud level (multiplied by Cloud Speed)
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND_ANGLE=Low Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_LOW_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Degrees the clouds move towards. 0 = east (+X), 90 = south (+Z)
option.CLOUD_FRACTUS=Thin Fragments
option.CLOUD_FRACTUS.comment=Thin torn wisps scattered in loose groups around the main clouds. 0 turns them off
option.CLOUD_MID_ALTITUDE=Mid Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_MID_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the mid cloud base. 0 = automatic (real proportions above the low clouds)
option.CLOUD_MID_THICKNESS=Mid Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_MID_THICKNESS.comment=Custom height template only. Blocks. 0 = automatic (real 900 m)
option.CLOUD_MID_COVERAGE=Mid Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_MID_COVERAGE.comment=Multiplier on the amount of altocumulus and altostratus
option.CLOUD_MID_DENSITY=Mid Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_MID_SCALE=Mid Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_MID_EROSION=Mid Cloud Erosion
option.CLOUD_MID_EROSION.comment=Lower gives smooth rounded patches, higher breaks them into small ragged lumps
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND=Mid Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND.comment=m/s at the mid cloud level (multiplied by Cloud Speed)
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND_ANGLE=Mid Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_MID_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Degrees the clouds move towards. 0 = east (+X), 90 = south (+Z)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_ALTITUDE=High Cloud Altitude
option.CLOUD_HIGH_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the bottom of the cirrus layer. 0 = automatic (real 8.4 km)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_THICKNESS=High Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_HIGH_THICKNESS.comment=Custom height template only. Blocks. 0 = automatic (real 1.4 km)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_DENSITY=High Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_HIGH_DENSITY.comment=Opacity of cirrus, cirrocumulus and cirrostratus
option.CLOUD_HIGH_SCALE=High Cloud Size
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND=High Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND.comment=m/s at the cirrus level (multiplied by Cloud Speed)
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND_ANGLE=High Wind Direction
option.CLOUD_HIGH_WIND_ANGLE.comment=Degrees. Cirrus streaks line up with this direction
option.CLOUD_CB_HEIGHT=Cumulonimbus Top
option.CLOUD_CB_HEIGHT.comment=Custom height template only. World y of the anvil top. 0 = automatic (real 10.2 km)
option.CLOUD_CB_COVERAGE=Storm Cells
option.CLOUD_CB_COVERAGE.comment=How many cumulonimbus cells form in thunderstorms and on stormy afternoons
option.CLOUD_CB_DENSITY=Cumulonimbus Density
option.CLOUD_CB_ANVIL=Anvil Length
option.CLOUD_CB_ANVIL.comment=How far the anvil spreads downwind. 0 keeps it over the tower
option.CLOUD_CB_RAIN_SHAFTS=Rain Shafts
option.CLOUD_CB_RAIN_SHAFTS.comment=Density of the grey rain curtains under storm cores. 0 turns them off
option.CLOUD_EDGE_SOFTNESS=Edge Softness
option.CLOUD_EDGE_SOFTNESS.comment=Width of the thin, soft margin of low clouds. Higher looks fluffier, lower looks crisper
option.CLOUD_EDGE_HAZE=Edge Haze
option.CLOUD_EDGE_HAZE.comment=Thin haze spreading out from the edges of fair-weather cumulus. 0 gives crisp outlines
option.CLOUD_CORE_STRENGTH=Core Density
option.CLOUD_CORE_STRENGTH.comment=Density of the centres of fair-weather cumulus bodies (small fragments and small clouds get half). Higher looks more solid with deeper shading between the lobes. 0.25 gives thin cores, 2.0 and above is almost uniformly dense
option.CLOUD_SILVER_LINING=Silver Lining
option.CLOUD_SILVER_LINING.comment=Glow of cloud edges backlit by the sun or moon
option.CLOUD_POWDER=Dark Edges
option.CLOUD_POWDER.comment=Darkening of thin edges with the sun behind you (powder effect)
option.CLOUD_AMBIENT=Sky Light in Clouds
option.CLOUD_AMBIENT.comment=Blue sky light inside clouds. Higher lifts the shaded sides
option.CLOUD_BASE_SHADE=Base Darkness
option.CLOUD_BASE_SHADE.comment=How grey the bottoms of thick clouds get
option.CLOUD_DRAW_DISTANCE=Cloud Draw Distance
option.CLOUD_DRAW_DISTANCE.comment=Kilometres at real scale for low and mid clouds. Shorter is faster
option.CLOUD_C_MID.comment=Custom climate only. Average amount of altocumulus and altostratus (varies by day)
option.CLOUD_C_HIGH.comment=Custom climate only. Average amount of cirrus (varies by day)

# Fog
option.FOG_STYLE=Fog Style
option.FOG_STYLE.comment=Shape and balance of the fog layers. Ray: physically based, a haze layer with a flat top, morning fog banks and valley mist. Bliss-like: denser haze and distance fade, more fog banks, mist also in the evening and at night, and a strong glow on the sun side. Nostalgia-like: no fog bank, haze that thins out gradually with height, a light distance fade, mist only in the morning and in rain. Custom: the sliders in Custom Fog Style. Distant air always fades into the horizon sky of the same direction. Overall strength is set by Fog Density and the Look preset
value.FOG_STYLE.0=Ray (Physical)
value.FOG_STYLE.1=Bliss-like
value.FOG_STYLE.2=Nostalgia-like
value.FOG_STYLE.3=Custom
screen.FOG_STYLE_SCREEN=Custom Fog Style
option.FOG_C_HAZE=Haze
option.FOG_C_HAZE.comment=Custom style only. Multiplies the haze density
option.FOG_C_EDGE=Distance Fade
option.FOG_C_EDGE.comment=Custom style only. Optical depth of the haze at the edge of the render distance. 0.6 leaves about 55% of the terrain visible, higher fades the distance more
option.FOG_C_LAYER=Fog Layer
option.FOG_C_LAYER.comment=Custom style only. Multiplies the density of the mid-level fog layer
option.FOG_C_GROUND=Ground Mist
option.FOG_C_GROUND.comment=Custom style only. Multiplies the density of the ground mist
option.FOG_C_FORWARD=Sunlit Glow
option.FOG_C_FORWARD.comment=Custom style only. How brightly sunlit haze and fog glow toward the sun (multiplies Light Shaft Strength)
option.FOG_BIOME=Biome Fog
option.FOG_BIOME.comment=Swamps and jungles get more fog and mist, deserts and badlands only dusty haze, snowy biomes thinner haze, oceans less valley mist
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Multiplies the Look preset value (1 with Natural)
option.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET=Fog Height Template
option.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.comment=Heights of the haze, the mid-level fog layer and the ground mist for worlds of different height. Vanilla: haze up to y 143 at noon, fog layer y 70-105, mist up to y 71. Tall World: haze up to y 406, fog layer y 90-200. Realistic: 1 block = 1 m (haze 1.1 km, fog layer 100-440 m). Custom: the sliders in Fog Heights. Match Clouds: follows the Cloud Height Template (the haze top stays at 3/4 of the cloud base)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.0=Vanilla (-64 to 320)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.1=Tall World (~2000)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.2=Realistic (1 block = 1 m)
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.3=Custom
value.FOG_HEIGHT_PRESET.4=Match Clouds
screen.FOG_HEIGHT_SCREEN=Fog Heights
option.FOG_C_SEA_LEVEL=Sea Level
option.FOG_C_SEA_LEVEL.comment=Custom template only. The height the haze and fog are measured from
option.FOG_C_HAZE_TOP=Haze Top
option.FOG_C_HAZE_TOP.comment=Custom template only. Top of the haze at noon (lower in the morning and at night). 0 = 3/4 of the cloud base
option.FOG_C_LAYER_BASE=Fog Layer Base
option.FOG_C_LAYER_BASE.comment=Custom template only. Bottom of the mid-level fog layer
option.FOG_C_LAYER_THICKNESS=Fog Layer Thickness
option.FOG_C_LAYER_THICKNESS.comment=Custom template only
option.FOG_LAYER=Fog Layer
option.FOG_LAYER.comment=Patches of fog at mid height (y 70-105 in Vanilla) with a flat top. Most common in the morning and on humid days, and spreads wide in rain. Light shafts show best inside it. Slightly heavier
option.FOG_MIST=Ground Mist
option.FOG_MIST.comment=Radiation fog that pools in valleys and over water at night, peaks at dawn and burns off about two hours after sunrise. Thicker on clear, humid days and after rain
option.FOG_MIST_ALTITUDE=Mist Altitude
option.FOG_MIST_ALTITUDE.comment=Custom template only. Top of the ground mist
option.VL=Volumetric Light
option.VL_SAMPLES=Volumetric Samples
option.VL_RES=Volumetric Resolution
value.VL_RES.1=Full
value.VL_RES.2=Half
value.VL_RES.4=Quarter
option.VL_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.VL_COLORED_SHADOWS=Colored Light Shafts
option.FOG_BLOCKLIGHT=Block Light Fog
option.FOG_BLOCKLIGHT.comment=Torches and other lights illuminate the fog.
option.FOG_BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light Fog Strength
option.FOG_CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadowed Light Shafts
option.VL_FAR=Distant Light Shafts
option.VL_FAR.comment=Light shafts beyond the shadow distance, traced in screen space from hills, trees and buildings. Only matters when the render distance is longer than the shadow distance. Slightly heavier
option.CAVE_LEAK_PREVENTION=Cave Light Leak Prevention
option.CAVE_LEAK_PREVENTION.comment=Keeps sunlight and light shafts out of places with no skylight, such as caves, even when the shadow map has a gap above them. Also dims far fog in caves. Can darken the far end of side tunnels and deep sea floors
option.GODRAYS=Screen-Space God Rays
option.GODRAYS.comment=Streaks of light from the sky around the sun or moon through gaps in trees, hills and buildings, drawn radially on screen. Stronger in thicker fog. Slightly heavier
option.GODRAYS_STRENGTH=Screen-Space God Ray Strength
option.GODRAYS_STRENGTH.comment=Default is 1.5. 1.0 is subtle and the streaks are faint
option.GODRAYS_RES=Screen-Space God Ray Resolution
value.GODRAYS_RES.2=Half
value.GODRAYS_RES.4=Quarter
option.GODRAYS_SAMPLES=Screen-Space God Ray Samples
option.GODRAYS_SAMPLES.comment=Higher values give smoother streaks; lower values add fine noise
option.BORDER_FOG=Border Fog
option.NETHER_FOG_DENSITY=Nether Fog Density
option.END_FOG_DENSITY=End Fog Density

# Camera
option.DOF=Depth of Field
option.DOF_QUALITY=DoF Quality
value.DOF_QUALITY.0=30 samples
value.DOF_QUALITY.1=50 samples
value.DOF_QUALITY.2=75 samples
option.DOF_QUALITY.comment=Large bokeh automatically uses more samples to avoid dots and rings (up to 256 / 384 / 512)
option.DOF_STRENGTH=Bokeh Amount
option.DOF_STRENGTH.comment=Aperture size when Aperture Control is Bokeh Amount. 0.5 = about f/2.1 (FOV 70). Doubling it roughly doubles the blur. For macro-like bokeh use 4 or more with a close focus
option.DOF_APERTURE_MODE=Aperture Control
value.DOF_APERTURE_MODE.0=Bokeh Amount
value.DOF_APERTURE_MODE.1=Lens Wide-Open f-number
value.DOF_APERTURE_MODE.2=Custom f-number
option.DOF_APERTURE_MODE.comment=Lens Wide-Open uses the lens preset's f-number (Modern prime f/1.8, Takumar f/1.4, ...). The focal length comes from the FOV, so FOV 70 is a 17mm wide angle and blurs much less than a 50mm lens (use a larger sensor for more blur). With Camera exposure the exposure f-number is always used
option.DOF_F_NUMBER=f-number
option.DOF_F_NUMBER.comment=f-number for Custom f-number, and for exposure and depth of field with Camera M and A (never wider than the lens preset's wide-open f-number). Camera P and S choose it automatically. Smaller blurs more
