option.EXPOSURE_ISO=ISO
option.EXPOSURE_ISO.comment=Sensitivity for Camera exposure. Twice the ISO is one stop brighter. Only changes brightness (with the Analog filter, a higher ISO also raises the gain noise). In the automatic Camera modes with Auto ISO, this is the lowest ISO
option.EXPOSURE_ISO_AUTO=Auto ISO
option.EXPOSURE_ISO_AUTO.comment=For Camera P, A and S. Keeps the ISO setting while there is enough light and raises the ISO only when the shutter would get slower than the slow limit (the same order as Canon, Nikon, Sony and Fujifilm cameras in P and A). At the maximum ISO it uses slower shutter speeds. In S it raises the ISO once the lens is wide open. Camera M has its own switch (Auto ISO in M)
option.EXPOSURE_ISO_AUTO_M=Auto ISO in M
option.EXPOSURE_ISO_AUTO_M.comment=For Camera M. Keeps your shutter speed and f-number and sets the ISO for the right exposure, from the ISO setting up to Auto ISO Maximum. Exposure compensation changes the ISO (like Canon and Nikon). The ISO blinks when it reaches either end. Off: M uses the ISO setting as before
