# Analog
option.ANALOG=Analog
option.ANALOG.comment=Makes the image look like footage from a 2000s consumer CCD camcorder (MiniDV / HDV). Pick the effects and the camera preset on the Analog screen. Off stops all of the extra processing
screen.ANALOG=Analog
screen.ANALOG.comment=Effects along a CCD camcorder's signal path (sensor -> noise -> in-camera processing -> recording). All of them need Analog
option.ANALOG_PRESET=Camera
option.ANALOG_PRESET.comment=Picks the camcorder's character (smear strength and so on). The per-effect on/off switches apply with every camera. The detail values can be changed under each effect only with Custom. Standard MiniDV: a faint streak through the sun. Cheap Compact: a small sensor with slightly stronger streaks. Low-Light Auto Gain: aimed at noise in dark scenes. Old Digital8: an older camera with a clear white line through the sun. HDV 1080i: a 3CCD HDV camera with barely visible streaks. PAL MiniDV: 50 Hz DV. Needs Analog
value.ANALOG_PRESET.0=Custom
value.ANALOG_PRESET.1=Standard MiniDV
value.ANALOG_PRESET.2=Cheap Compact Camcorder
value.ANALOG_PRESET.3=Low-Light Auto Gain
value.ANALOG_PRESET.4=Old Digital8
value.ANALOG_PRESET.5=HDV 1080i
value.ANALOG_PRESET.6=PAL MiniDV
screen.ANALOG_SENSOR=Sensor
screen.ANALOG_SENSOR.comment=Effects of the CCD sensor. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_SMEAR=Vertical Smear
option.ANALOG_SMEAR.comment=A faint streak runs up and down to the screen edges through the column that holds the sun (the CCD keeps adding charge from the bright light while it reads out). The streak scales with the column's average brightness, so columns of plain sky barely lift. Torches and other lights only streak where they cluster or appear large up close. The strength comes from the camera preset. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_RATIO=Smear Ratio
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_RATIO.comment=Custom camera only. Streak to signal ratio (%) for a uniformly lit column. Real consumer sensors are around 0.01 %, but the in-game sun is dimmer than the real one, so 0.1 % gives a faint streak and 1.0 % a clear white line. Higher is a brighter streak
suffix.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_RATIO= %
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_TINT_MODE=Smear Color
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_TINT_MODE.comment=Custom camera only. White: a white streak like real cameras (the column's average brightness). Light Color: the streak takes the color of the light in the column, such as orange at sunset
value.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_TINT_MODE.0=Light Color
value.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_TINT_MODE.1=White
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_SHUTTER_STOPS=Smear Exposure Link
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_SHUTTER_STOPS.comment=Custom camera only. How many stops the shutter speeds up in bright scenes, strengthening the streak. Relative to night and caves, up to 2^stops times stronger in clear daylight. 0 does not follow exposure. With Camera exposure or Shutter Speed Effect, the shutter speed sets it instead (stronger than 1/60 s by the same limit)
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_LIGHT_THRESHOLD=Light Smear Threshold
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_LIGHT_THRESHOLD.comment=Custom camera only. Only the part of a torch or other light brighter than this (times white after exposure) makes a streak. Raise it to keep streaks to clustered lights and lights seen up close
option.ANALOG_SMEAR_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Light Smear Strength
option.ANALOG_SMEAR_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Applies with every camera. Multiplier for the streaks of torches and other lights (on top of the camera's light gain). 0 turns light streaks off. Does not affect the sun's streak
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_LIGHT_GAIN=Light Smear Gain
option.ANALOG_C_SMEAR_LIGHT_GAIN.comment=Custom camera only. Multiplier for the part of a light above the threshold (in-game lights are dimmer than real ones, so a large factor is needed for a streak). 0 turns light streaks off. Does not affect the sun's streak. To raise it while keeping a camera preset, use Light Smear Strength
option.ANALOG_BLOOMING=Blooming
option.ANALOG_BLOOMING.comment=When a CCD pixel saturates, the excess charge spills into the pixels above and below in the same column, crushing the area above and below bright lights or the sun to white (unlike the faint smear streak, only the nearby part blows out). Invisible while the camera's value is 0 (raise it with Cheap Compact, Old Digital8 or Custom). Costs 8 reads per pixel. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_BLOOMING_LENGTH=Blooming Length
option.ANALOG_C_BLOOMING_LENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. How far the overflow reaches up and down (in scan lines). 0 turns it off
option.ANALOG_C_BLOOMING_THRESHOLD=Blooming Threshold
option.ANALOG_C_BLOOMING_THRESHOLD.comment=Custom camera only. Brightness where the overflow starts. 1 = the recording limit (the top of the knee when Knee is on, white when off). Lower it to make slightly bright objects spill too
option.ANALOG_RESOLUTION=Resolution
option.ANALOG_RESOLUTION.comment=Lowers detail to the recording format's pixel count (720 wide for DV) and scan lines for a softer image. Applies to brightness only. Costs 8 reads per pixel. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_RESOLUTION_H=Horizontal Softness
option.ANALOG_C_RESOLUTION_H.comment=Custom camera only. 1 = the format's pixel count. Higher is softer horizontally
option.ANALOG_C_RESOLUTION_V=Vertical Softness
option.ANALOG_C_RESOLUTION_V.comment=Custom camera only. 1 = the scan lines (the detail interlaced video actually shows). Higher is softer vertically
screen.ANALOG_NOISE=Noise
screen.ANALOG_NOISE.comment=Image sensor noise. It grows in darker scenes as the auto gain rises. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_NOISE=Sensor Noise
option.ANALOG_NOISE.comment=Switches the shot, dark, color, fixed pattern and hot pixel noise together. Film grain is not applied while this is on. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_NOISE_STRENGTH=Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_NOISE_STRENGTH.comment=Applies with every camera. Multiplier for all five kinds of noise. 0 removes the noise (and its cost)
option.ANALOG_C_AGC_MAX=Auto Gain Limit
option.ANALOG_C_AGC_MAX.comment=Custom camera only. How far (in stops) the camera raises its sensitivity in dark scenes. Higher gives more noise in the dark. With Camera exposure the ISO sets the gain instead (gain = ISO / 100, keeps rising with ISO)
option.ANALOG_C_AGC_EV=Auto Gain Start
option.ANALOG_C_AGC_EV.comment=Custom camera only. The gain starts rising when the scene exposure (applied EV) is darker than this. Clear daylight is about 0, caves about -1, a village at night about -2.5
option.ANALOG_SHOT_NOISE=Shot Noise
option.ANALOG_SHOT_NOISE.comment=Fluctuation in the number of light particles: fine grain in midtones and highlights. Needs Analog and Sensor Noise
option.ANALOG_C_SHOT_NOISE_STRENGTH=Shot Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_C_SHOT_NOISE_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only
option.ANALOG_C_SHOT_NOISE_CHROMA=Shot Noise Color
option.ANALOG_C_SHOT_NOISE_CHROMA.comment=Custom camera only. 0 = brightness-only grain, 1 = separate grain per color channel
option.ANALOG_DARK_NOISE=Dark Noise
option.ANALOG_DARK_NOISE.comment=Readout and dark current noise amplified by the auto gain: graininess in the dark parts of dark scenes. Needs Analog and Sensor Noise
option.ANALOG_C_DARK_NOISE_STRENGTH=Dark Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_C_DARK_NOISE_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only
option.ANALOG_C_DARK_NOISE_SIZE=Dark Noise Grain Size
option.ANALOG_C_DARK_NOISE_SIZE.comment=Custom camera only. In format pixels
option.ANALOG_CHROMA_NOISE=Color Noise
option.ANALOG_CHROMA_NOISE.comment=Color blotches in shadows and dark scenes, shaped by the chroma subsampling (wide with 4:1:1). Needs Analog and Sensor Noise
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_NOISE_STRENGTH=Color Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_NOISE_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_NOISE_SHADOW=Color Noise Shadow Bias
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_NOISE_SHADOW.comment=Custom camera only. Higher keeps it to the dark parts. 0 ignores brightness
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_NOISE_SIZE=Color Noise Blotch Size
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_NOISE_SIZE.comment=Custom camera only. In chroma samples
option.ANALOG_FPN=Fixed Pattern Noise
option.ANALOG_FPN.comment=Per-pixel unevenness and per-column stripes of the image sensor. Fixed to the screen and only visible in dark scenes. Invisible while the camera's value is 0 (raise it with Low-Light Auto Gain, Cheap Compact, Old Digital8 or Custom). Needs Analog and Sensor Noise
option.ANALOG_C_FPN_STRENGTH=Fixed Pattern Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_C_FPN_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. 0 turns it off
option.ANALOG_C_FPN_COLUMN=Column Stripe Share
option.ANALOG_C_FPN_COLUMN.comment=Custom camera only. 0 = per-pixel unevenness only, 1 = column stripes only
option.ANALOG_HOT_PIXELS=Hot Pixels
option.ANALOG_HOT_PIXELS.comment=Defective pixels that glow white in dark scenes. Fixed to the screen. Invisible while the camera's value is 0 (raise it with Low-Light Auto Gain, Old Digital8 or Custom). Needs Analog and Sensor Noise
option.ANALOG_C_HOT_PIXELS_DENSITY=Hot Pixel Count
option.ANALOG_C_HOT_PIXELS_DENSITY.comment=Custom camera only. Share of pixels that become white dots. 0 turns it off
option.ANALOG_C_HOT_PIXELS_BRIGHTNESS=Hot Pixel Brightness
option.ANALOG_C_HOT_PIXELS_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Custom camera only
screen.ANALOG_PROCESS=Processing
screen.ANALOG_PROCESS.comment=In-camera image processing. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_KNEE=Knee and Clipping
option.ANALOG_KNEE.comment=The video camera knee. Highlights are rolled off gently and clipped at the recording limit; each color clips on its own, so bright colors wash out to white. Replaces the tone mapper (and the lava look adjustment). Off keeps the chosen tone mapper. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_KNEE_POINT=Knee Point
option.ANALOG_C_KNEE_POINT.comment=Custom camera only. Brightness where the highlights start to roll off (real cameras use 70-90 %, typically 80 %). Lower rolls off earlier and keeps more steps before clipping
option.ANALOG_C_KNEE_RANGE=Knee Range
option.ANALOG_C_KNEE_RANGE.comment=Custom camera only. How many stops of highlights the knee fits under the recording limit. Wider clips later but flattens the highlights
option.ANALOG_SHARPEN=Edge Enhancement
option.ANALOG_SHARPEN.comment=The camcorder's detail enhancement: edges get a white rim on the bright side and a dark rim on the dark side (halo). Applies to brightness only and leaves fine fluctuations alone. Costs 1 read per pixel. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_SHARPEN_STRENGTH=Edge Enhancement Strength
option.ANALOG_C_SHARPEN_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. Higher gives darker, brighter halos
option.ANALOG_C_SHARPEN_RADIUS=Halo Width
option.ANALOG_C_SHARPEN_RADIUS.comment=Custom camera only. Width of the rim in format pixels
option.ANALOG_C_SHARPEN_CORING=Coring
option.ANALOG_C_SHARPEN_CORING.comment=Custom camera only. Brightness differences smaller than this are not enhanced. Raise it to keep grain and fine patterns from being sharpened
screen.ANALOG_RECORD=Recording
screen.ANALOG_RECORD.comment=Effects of the tape recording format. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_FORMAT_MODE=Recording Format
option.ANALOG_C_FORMAT_MODE.comment=Custom camera only. Sets the pixel count, scan lines and chroma subsampling together. NTSC DV: 720x480, chroma at 1/4 width (4:1:1). PAL DV: 720x576, chroma at half width and half height (4:2:0). HDV 1080i: 1440x1080, 4:2:0
value.ANALOG_C_FORMAT_MODE.0=NTSC DV
value.ANALOG_C_FORMAT_MODE.1=PAL DV
value.ANALOG_C_FORMAT_MODE.2=HDV 1080i
option.ANALOG_CHROMA=Color Bleed
option.ANALOG_CHROMA.comment=Records only the color (chroma) coarsely as the format does, so red and blue edges bleed sideways (also vertically with 4:2:0). Brightness detail is kept. Costs 6 to 8 reads per pixel and building the screen mipmaps. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_STRENGTH=Color Bleed Strength
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. 1 = as the format records it. Lower mixes back the original color for a weaker bleed
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_UPSAMPLE_MODE=Color Reconstruction
option.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_UPSAMPLE_MODE.comment=Custom camera only. How the coarse color is spread back to pixels. Interpolate: smooth bleeding. Nearest: blocky steps at color edges
value.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_UPSAMPLE_MODE.0=Interpolate
value.ANALOG_C_CHROMA_UPSAMPLE_MODE.1=Nearest
option.ANALOG_BLOCK=Block Noise
option.ANALOG_BLOCK.comment=The 8x8 blocks of DV compression: steps at block borders and lost detail (and noise). The grid is fixed to the screen. More detail is lost while the view moves. Costs 4 reads per pixel (shared with mosquito noise). Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_BLOCK_STRENGTH=Block Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_C_BLOCK_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. How much detail is dropped. 0 turns it off
option.ANALOG_C_BLOCK_MOTION=Blocking in Motion
option.ANALOG_C_BLOCK_MOTION.comment=Custom camera only. How much more detail is lost where the view moves
option.ANALOG_MOSQUITO=Mosquito Noise
option.ANALOG_MOSQUITO.comment=Flickering fine specks around edges where compression errors spread. Flat areas stay clean. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_MOSQUITO_STRENGTH=Mosquito Noise Strength
option.ANALOG_C_MOSQUITO_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. 0 turns it off
option.ANALOG_C_MOSQUITO_EDGE=Mosquito Edge Threshold
option.ANALOG_C_MOSQUITO_EDGE.comment=Custom camera only. Edge strength where the specks start. Raise it to keep them to strong edges
option.ANALOG_DROPOUT=Dropouts
option.ANALOG_DROPOUT.comment=Tape damage drops the signal and scattered blocks briefly (about 1/15 s) show the previous frame. Only visible while the view moves. The rate comes from the camera (about once a minute on Standard and PAL MiniDV, about 20 times on Old Digital8, none on the others). Costs 1 read per pixel. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_C_DROPOUT_RATE=Dropout Rate
option.ANALOG_C_DROPOUT_RATE.comment=Custom camera only. Times per minute. 0 turns it off
option.ANALOG_C_DROPOUT_AMOUNT=Dropout Amount
option.ANALOG_C_DROPOUT_AMOUNT.comment=Custom camera only. Share of blocks hidden each time
option.ANALOG_INTERLACE=Interlacing
option.ANALOG_INTERLACE.comment=Captures each picture in two passes (even and odd scan lines 1/60 s apart). Moving the view makes moving parts split into a comb. Nothing shows while the view is still, and moving objects (mobs, water) do not comb. Costs 2 reads per pixel. Needs Analog
option.ANALOG_INTERLACE_MODE=Interlace Display
option.ANALOG_INTERLACE_MODE.comment=Applies with every camera. Weave: both fields side by side in one frame like DV viewed on a PC, combing when moving. Field: one field every 1/60 s like on a TV, with flickering fine horizontal lines
value.ANALOG_INTERLACE_MODE.0=Weave
value.ANALOG_INTERLACE_MODE.1=Field
option.ANALOG_C_INTERLACE_STRENGTH=Comb Width
option.ANALOG_C_INTERLACE_STRENGTH.comment=Custom camera only. 1 = the time between fields (1/60 s, 1/50 s for PAL). Higher gives a wider comb

